  "checks": [
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.pairings: E:terminal-wick-formula",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:65-73 defines maps satisfying 'p x ∈ S ∧ p x ≠ x ∧ p (p x) = x', identity outside S. TeX:3616-3622,3670-3673 uses unordered pair partitions of the labelled factors. The normalization counts each partition once. Ledger:1923 and claims.yaml:13518 agree."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.pairWeight: E:terminal-pairing-integral",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:75-79 defines '∏ x ∈ S with x < p x, c x (p x)'. TeX:3634-3638 has one covariance factor per unordered pair and coefficient one. Selecting the smaller endpoint is harmless for symmetric covariance. Ledger:1924 and claims.yaml:13525 agree."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.wickSum: E:terminal-wick-formula",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:81-83 defines '∑ p ∈ pairings S, pairWeight c S p'. TeX:3619-3622 sums over pair partitions, without extra coefficients. Ledger:1925 and claims.yaml:13532 faithfully describe this combinatorial component, not the integrated identity."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.mem_pairings: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:85-88 gives the exact membership equivalence. TeX:3670-3673 speaks of pair partitions but contains no function-encoding membership lemma. Ledger:1926 and claims.yaml:13539 match; no direct label is appropriate."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.pairings_empty: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:90-96 proves 'pairings ∅ = {id}', without additional hypotheses. TeX:3639 supplies the empty-product convention, not this encoding identity. Ledger:1927 and claims.yaml:13546 are faithful."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.wickSum_empty: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:98-100 proves 'wickSum c ∅ = 1' for every c. TeX:3639 says empty chains have the usual empty-product meaning. Ledger:1928 and claims.yaml:13553 correctly give the encoding-level identity without claiming a direct labelled theorem."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.unpair_a: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:103,108-111 assumes 'a ≠ b' and concludes 'unpair a b p a = a'. TeX:3664-3673 uses the generating-function route and has no update operation. Ledger:1929 and claims.yaml:13560 correctly identify a Lean-route auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.unpair_b: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:112-114 proves 'unpair a b p b = b' without a distinctness hypothesis. TeX:3664-3673 contains no corresponding update lemma. Ledger:1930 and claims.yaml:13567 preserve the quantifiers."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.unpair_other: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:115-118 assumes 'x ≠ a' and 'x ≠ b' and preserves p x. TeX:3664-3673 has no function-update counterpart. Ledger:1931 and claims.yaml:13574 accurately classify and state the auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.pairUp_a: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:106,119-122 assumes 'a ≠ b' and concludes 'pairUp a b q a = b'. TeX:3664-3673 has no such operation. Ledger:1932 and claims.yaml:13581 agree with the type."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.pairUp_b: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:123-125 proves 'pairUp a b q b = a' for arbitrary a,b,q. TeX:3664-3673 supplies no corresponding auxiliary. Ledger:1933 and claims.yaml:13588 are faithful."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.pairUp_other: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:126-129 assumes 'x ≠ a' and 'x ≠ b' and concludes equality with q x. TeX:3664-3673 has no function-update counterpart. Ledger:1934 and claims.yaml:13595 agree."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.fiber_sum: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:135-138 requires 'a ∈ S', '∀ x ∈ S, a ≤ x', and 'b ∈ S.erase a'; it factors the partner-b fiber as c a b times the smaller Wick sum. TeX:3664-3673 instead differentiates the generating function. Ledger:1935 and claims.yaml:13602 honestly mark this route auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.wickSum_eq_sum_erase: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:241-243 assumes a is a least member of S and expands along its partner. TeX:3664-3673 does not state this recursion. Ledger:1936 and claims.yaml:13609 state the exact identity without mislabelling it a TeX proof step."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.card_erase_erase: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:255-257 assumes 'a ∈ S' and 'b ∈ S.erase a' and proves cardinality S.card - 2. TeX:3664-3673 contains no such finite-set lemma. Ledger:1937 and claims.yaml:13616 agree."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.wickSum_odd: L:terminal-wick",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:260-261 assumes 'S.card = 2 * k + 1' and proves 'wickSum c S = 0' for arbitrary c. TeX:3638,3670 states odd total degree gives zero. Ledger:1938 explicitly calls this the pairing form of that step; claims.yaml:13623 agrees."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.wickSum_const_one: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:278-280 identifies the all-one Wick sum with the real coercion of the pairing count. TeX:3670-3673 has no standalone all-one calibration. Ledger:1939 and claims.yaml:13630 faithfully state an auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.wickSum_abs_le: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:285-286 assumes '∀ x y, |c x y| ≤ V' and 'S.card = 2 * k'; the bound is '(2*k-1)!! * V^k'. TeX:3651-3656 obtains the corresponding Gaussian product bound by Hölder, not this arbitrary-weight theorem. Ledger:1940 and claims.yaml:13637 correctly give no direct label."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.card_pairings_even: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:319-320 assumes cardinality 2k and proves exactly '(2*k-1).doubleFactorial' pairings. TeX:3671-3673 uses unordered partitions and cancellation of 2^k k!, consistently giving (2k-1)!!. Ledger:1941 and claims.yaml:13644 correctly record the count and k=0 convention."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.card_pairings_odd: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:349-353 assumes cardinality 2k+1 and concludes 'pairings S = ∅'. TeX:3670 states odd-degree vanishing, not this encoding-level set identity. Ledger:1942 and claims.yaml:13651 agree."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.wickSum_nonneg: L:terminal-wick",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:356-358 assumes '∀ x y, 0 ≤ c x y'. TeX:3693-3694 assumes 'K ≥ 0' and makes each covariance product nonnegative. Ledger:1943 correctly identifies the pointwise step; claims.yaml:13658 matches."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.wickSum_mono: L:terminal-wick",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:361-364 assumes '0 ≤ c₁' and 'c₁ ≤ c₂' entrywise. TeX:3641,3694-3695 uses '0 ≤ K₁ ≤ K₂'. Ledger:1944 and claims.yaml:13665 faithfully state the pointwise comparison step."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.one_le_matBound: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:372,376-379 defines matBound as '1 + ∑ c, ∑ k, |A c k|' and proves it is at least one for every real square A. TeX:3664-3673 has no such growth constant. Ledger:1945 and claims.yaml:13672 correctly classify this auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.mulVec_apply_eq: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:383-384 states '(A *ᵥ g) c = ∑ k, A c k * g k', with no analytic hypotheses. TeX:3664-3673 has no matrix-vector expansion in its proof route. Ledger:1946 and claims.yaml:13679 agree."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.abs_mulVec_le: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:388-389 bounds '|(A *ᵥ g) c|' by 'matBound A * (1 + ‖g‖)', using the function-space sup norm. TeX:3664-3673 has no corresponding growth estimate. Ledger:1947 and claims.yaml:13686 preserve the norm convention."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.abs_prod_mulVec_le: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:409-413 gives the monomial bound with exponents T.card and no additional hypotheses. TeX:3664-3673 has no polynomial-growth auxiliary of this form. Ledger:1948 and claims.yaml:13693 match."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.continuous_mulVec_apply: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:417-420 proves continuity of 'g ↦ (A *ᵥ g) c' for arbitrary real A,c. TeX:3664-3673 does not state this route auxiliary. Ledger:1949 and claims.yaml:13700 agree."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.continuous_prod_mulVec: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:424-426 proves continuity of each finite monomial in A g. TeX:3664-3673 has no corresponding continuity lemma. Ledger:1950 and claims.yaml:13707 correctly state the auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.hasDerivAt_mulVec_update: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:430-436 proves the slice derivative is 'A c e' at every real t. TeX:3664-3673 differentiates a generating function, not coordinate slices of A g. Ledger:1951 and claims.yaml:13714 correctly give no direct label."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.hasDerivAt_prod_update: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:440-449 defines monoDeriv and proves the derivative at 'Function.update x e t'. TeX:3664-3673 has no corresponding monomial slice calculation. Ledger:1952 and claims.yaml:13721 preserve the evaluation point."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.abs_monoDeriv_le: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:458-461 gives exactly 'T.card * matBound A * matBound A ^ T.card' times '(1 + ‖y‖)^T.card'. TeX:3664-3673 contains no such auxiliary constant. Ledger:1953 and claims.yaml:13728 match."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.integrable_prod_mulVec: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:493-496 proves Integrable of every finite monomial under stdPi, for arbitrary real A,j,T. TeX:3664-3673 does not state this change-of-model integrability lemma. Ledger:1954 and claims.yaml:13735 are faithful."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.continuous_monoDeriv: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:500-503 proves 'Continuous (monoDeriv A j T e)' without extra assumptions. TeX:3664-3673 has no monoDeriv object. Ledger:1955 and claims.yaml:13742 correctly classify the route auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.wick_stdPi: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:513-515 assumes 'S.card = n' and gives the monomial integral as the Wick sum for A Aᵀ, for every n. TeX:3664-3673 gives the general Gaussian identity by a different route, not this stdPi representation theorem. Ledger:1956 and claims.yaml:13749 agree; monomial integrability is separately proved at 493-496."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.sqrt_mul_transpose: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:567-573 requires 'K.PosSemidef' and proves 'CFC.sqrt K * (CFC.sqrt K)ᵀ = K'. TeX:3664-3673 uses covariance directly, without this square-root bridge. Ledger:1957 and claims.yaml:13756 correctly record an auxiliary identity."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.integral_multivariateGaussian_eq: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:578-583 requires only 'Continuous F', with arbitrary K, and equates the two totalized integrals. TeX:3664-3673 has no arbitrary-continuous-F bridge. Ledger:1958 and claims.yaml:13763 accurately state the type. The separate paragraph's claim that all such integrals are genuine is false; see W2."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.integrable_multivariateGaussian_iff: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:586-592 requires 'Continuous F' and proves an integrability equivalence, not integrability itself. TeX:3664-3673 has no such bridge. Ledger:1959 and claims.yaml:13770 preserve that distinction."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.wick_multivariateGaussian: L:terminal-wick",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:599-602 assumes 'K.PosSemidef' and concludes both monomial integrability and the Wick formula. TeX:3601-3602,3662-3673 assumes a centered real Gaussian vector with covariance K; positive semidefiniteness is inherent. Ledger:1960 and claims.yaml:13777 faithfully map the Gaussian step."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.wick_hasLaw: L:terminal-wick",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:618-622 assumes 'K.PosSemidef' and 'HasLaw Xv (multivariateGaussian 0 K) P'. TeX:3601-3602,3662-3673 assumes the same finite-dimensional centered Gaussian law. HasLaw forces probability mass one, so no missing separate probability assumption changes the object. Ledger:1961 and claims.yaml:13784 agree."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.CenteredGaussianField: L:terminal-wick",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:642-646 requires positive semidefiniteness and the centered multivariate Gaussian law for every finite family, including repetitions. TeX:3601-3602 says 'centered real Gaussian field ... with covariance K'. These are matching finite-dimensional requirements. Ledger:1962 and claims.yaml:13791 are accurate."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.CenteredGaussianField.wick: L:terminal-wick",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:652-655 assumes CenteredGaussianField and arbitrary finite point/index families, and proves integrability plus the pairing sum. TeX:3662-3673 applies Wick to the Gaussian variables at labelled vertices. Ledger:1963 and claims.yaml:13798 faithfully describe that pointwise identity."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.CenteredGaussianField.wick_univ: L:terminal-wick",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:660-664 specializes to all labels of Fin n, preserving integrability. TeX:3662-3673 differentiates once for each labelled factor. Ledger:1964 and claims.yaml:13805 match; no independence or distinct-point assumption is added."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.CenteredGaussianField.symm: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:667-670 assumes CenteredGaussianField and proves 'K y x = K x y'. TeX:3601-3602 makes K a covariance but states no separate symmetry lemma. Ledger:1965 and claims.yaml:13812 correctly use no direct label."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.CenteredGaussianField.abs_le: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:674-675 assumes '∀ x, K x x ≤ V' and concludes '|K x y| ≤ V'. TeX:3602-3603 assumes the finite supremum of variances; the bound is its covariance consequence. Ledger:1966 and claims.yaml:13819 correctly state this auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.CenteredGaussianField.wick_append: L:terminal-wick",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:690-694 assumes only the centered Gaussian field law and two finite tuples, and gives integrability plus the Wick sum for 'Fin.append p q'. TeX:3616-3618,3662-3673 concatenates the two chains without joining their Green measures. Ledger:1967 and claims.yaml:13826 agree."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.FiniteWick.CenteredGaussianField.sq_moment_le: L:terminal-wick",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "FiniteWick.lean:707-710 assumes the Gaussian field and diagonal variance bound, proving square integrability and '(2n-1)!! * V^n'. TeX:3652-3656 gives the square-root version under the same bound. Ledger:1968 explicitly records the different Wick/count proof route; claims.yaml:13833 matches."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TerminalWick.chainWeight: E:terminal-chain-measure",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "TerminalWick.lean:110-114 defines the ordered-time product of Green total masses, not a measure on space-time tuples. TeX:3586-3598 defines the actual backward spatial pushforward measure. Ledger:5916 and claims.yaml:13842 explicitly restrict the correspondence to its mass integrand and say the identifying mass equality is not proved."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TerminalWick.chainWeight_eq: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "TerminalWick.lean:124-125 assumes 'd = 1 ∨ d = 2 ∨ d = 3' and identifies the weight with the ofReal time-gap recursion. TeX:3648 says 'The mass of G_h is h', but has no equality between these two Lean encodings. Ledger:5917 and claims.yaml:13849 correctly identify an auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TerminalWick.measurable_chainWeightReal: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "TerminalWick.lean:138-139 proves joint measurability of '(T,s) ↦ chainWeightReal n T s' for every n. TeX:3648-3651 does not state this encoding-level measurability result. Ledger:5918 and claims.yaml:13856 agree."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TerminalWick.chainMassReal_succ: L:terminal-wick",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "TerminalWick.lean:158-159 states 'M_(n+1)(T) = ∫⁻ t in Ioo 0 T, ofReal(T-t) * M_n(t)' for every real T. TeX:3648-3650 states the same last-vertex recursion at positive horizons. Ledger:5919 and claims.yaml:13863 accurately explain the lower-integral encoding."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TerminalWick.chainMassReal_eq: L:terminal-wick",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "TerminalWick.lean:192-193 assumes '0 ≤ T' and proves 'ofReal (T^(2*n)/(2*n)!)'. TeX:3650-3651 gives exactly T^(2n)/(2n)!. Ledger:5920 and claims.yaml:13870 preserve the factorial and exponent."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TerminalWick.aestronglyMeasurable_prod: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "TerminalWick.lean:228-232 assumes CenteredGaussianField and a fixed tuple z and proves measurability in omega. TeX:3657-3659 concerns strong measurability in the chain variables, a different assertion. Ledger:5921 and claims.yaml:13877 correctly avoid that direct mapping."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TerminalWick.memLp_prod: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "TerminalWick.lean:235-238 assumes the Gaussian field law and concludes 'MemLp ... 2 P' at each fixed tuple. TeX:3652-3659 bounds these products but has no separate MemLp encoding statement. Ledger:5922 and claims.yaml:13884 match."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TerminalWick.prodL2: L:terminal-wick",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "TerminalWick.lean:242-243 defines the Lp class of the ordinary scalar product using proved MemLp. TeX:3607 integrates '∏ W(s_j,y_j)' in L². Ledger:5923 and claims.yaml:13891 identify the same integrand, not a Wick-renormalized product."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TerminalWick.coeFn_prodL2: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "TerminalWick.lean:246-248 proves the Lp representative equals the scalar product P-almost everywhere. TeX:3607 has no quotient-representative lemma. Ledger:5924 and claims.yaml:13898 accurately state this bridge."
    },
    {
